WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
-----------------------------------------

COVERED — everything in this repository that is ours:

  * the Android application under android/
  * the research library, experiment code and scripts under research/ and scripts/
  * the figures and tables under results/
  * the written documents under docs/, paper/ and ux/

NOT COVERED — third-party material, under its own separate terms:

  * DATASETS. No dataset is distributed in this repository. HMOG, FETA,
    Tappigraphy and the rest are obtained from their own sources using the DOIs
    in docs/DATASETS.md, and each carries its own licence. In particular, the
    HMOG terms of use permit NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH ONLY, FORBID
    REDISTRIBUTION, and REQUIRE ATTRIBUTION in publications. A licence on this
    code grants you nothing with respect to that data.

  * PAPERS. The PDFs under references/papers/ are third-party publications and
    are not distributed here.

  * REFERENCE CODE. research/reference-code/ contains repositories written by
    other researchers. Each has its own licence and its own upstream home, and
    none of it is distributed here.


A NOTE ON WHAT THIS SOFTWARE IS
--------------------------------

PRECOG is a research prototype. It describes how a person's scrolling compares
to their own earlier scrolling.

It is not a medical device, a diagnostic instrument, or a clinical tool. It does
not detect addiction, compulsion, or any disorder, and none of the behavioural
states it reports are clinical findings. No detection-accuracy figure is claimed
for it, because none has been measured on the features it actually observes.

Both licences below disclaim warranties and liability, and that disclaimer is
meant seriously here: do not deploy this to make decisions about people.
